# Coding Guidelines

- Follow the installed Next.js 16 docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.
- Route Handlers perform transport concerns only: auth, validation, invocation, HTTP mapping.
- Put business rules in application/domain services and persistence in repositories.
- Validate untrusted input with Zod and return DTOs, never Prisma records.
- Avoid `any`, non-null assertions, silent catches, magic values, and unbounded operations.
- Use dependency injection through explicit factories/composition roots for ports.
- Use structured domain/application errors and one consistent HTTP error mapper.
- External calls need timeouts; retry only safe/idempotent operations with bounds.
- Preserve accessibility and use existing UI primitives/tokens.
- Relative TS imports inside `packages/*` must not use `.js` extensions, except generated Prisma JS.
- Add focused tests for changed behavior and concurrency-sensitive invariants.
